# ltpadmin(1) startup for the LUNAR GATEWAY node: LTP engine 50.
# Two spans. Each LSO sends to the link emulator port for that direction:
#   gateway->rover  127.0.0.1:25099 -> rover udplsi 127.0.0.1:19913
#   gateway->earth  127.0.0.1:25023 -> earth udplsi 127.0.0.1:12313
#   a span <peer> <max export sessions> <max import sessions> <max segment size>
#          <aggregation size threshold> <aggregation time limit> '<LSO cmd>' [<queuing latency>]
# Aggregation size threshold 1 byte: every bundle is sent as its own LTP block
# as soon as ltpclo dequeues it, so a small bundle never waits for the
# aggregation time limit (1 s, checked once per second by ltpclock) at each
# hop. Bundles not yet dequeued wait in the BP egress plan's queues (bulk,
# standard, urgent). At most 32 blocks (export sessions) per span are open
# at a time.
# Delivery backlog: while this many received blocks wait for delivery to BP,
# ION discards every further red segment, checkpoints included (ltprc(5)
# 'm maxbacklog', default 10; counted as in_seg_too_fast), and each discarded
# checkpoint costs the sender a checkpoint timeout. The limit is set to the
# blocks the peers can have open towards this node at once (32 import
# sessions per span, two spans = 64), so a full window of blocks completing
# together, as after a scheduled outage, stays below the limit.
1 64
a span 99 32 32 1024 1 1 'udplso 127.0.0.1:25099' 1
a span 23 32 32 1024 1 1 'udplso 127.0.0.1:25023' 1
a seat 'udplsi 127.0.0.1:15013'
m maxbacklog 64
s
